<decision #track.topological_decision_questions.frontier_batches apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M02EGVAZX2K0VZ036CGW46N3>
  How should planning ask a decision forest with multiple roots?
  </?01M02EGVAZX2K0VZ036CGW46N3>
  <answer ?01M02EGVAZX2K0VZ036CGW46N4>
  Ask every independently answerable root or unlocked child in one bounded topological batch, then recompute after the response.
  </?01M02EGVAZX2K0VZ036CGW46N4>
  <evidence ?01M02EGVAZX2K0VZ036CGW46N5>
  The requested protocol must avoid serialising unrelated decision directions while retaining dependency order.
